{"name":"Orange Ballad","hex":"#b56d41","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"},{"term":"ballad","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of narrative poem, adapted for recitation or singing; especially, a sentimental or romantic poem in short stanzas.","A slow romantic song."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make mention of in ballads.","To compose or sing ballads."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballad","blocks":[{"text":"A ballad is a form of verse, often a narrative set to music. Ballads were particularly characteristic of the popular poetry and song of England, Ireland and Scotland from the Late Middle Ages until the 19th century. They were widely used across Europe, and later in Australia, North Africa, North America and South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Maria_Wiik_-_Ballad.jpg/330px-Maria_Wiik_-_Ballad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballad","wikidata":"Q182659"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Here_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png/330px-Here_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Here_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png/330px-Here_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sixteenth-century printed ballad, the A Gest of Robyn Hode","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHere_begynneth_a_gest_of_Robyn_Hode.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Scott%27s_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG/500px-Scott%27s_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Scott%27s_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG/1280px-Scott%27s_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Scott%27s_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG/500px-Scott%27s_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Walter Scott's Minstrelsy of the Scottish Border","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScott's_Minstrelsy_Of_The_Scottish_Border.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/The-Twa-Corbies.jpg/500px-The-Twa-Corbies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/